asahi-diagnose: support Slackware

package_versions() recognises only /etc/arch-release and /etc/fedora-release.
On any other distribution it prints

  Distribution not supported

and returns, so the package list -- the section a support request is usually
asking for -- comes back empty. Everything else in the report is correct: the
device information, firmware versions and boot configuration all read from the
device tree and are distribution-agnostic.

Slackware has no query command that accepts a list of package names, so the
`cmd="pacman -Q"` / `cmd="rpm -q"` shape the function is built around has
nothing to bind to. Rather than special-case the output block, this adds a
shell function that stands in for such a command: the existing
`$($cmd $pkgs 2>/dev/null | sort -u)` call is left untouched, since an unquoted
expansion invokes a function just as it would a binary.

The matching needs one piece of care. A Slackware package file is named

  name-version-arch-build

and only the NAME may contain hyphens -- version, arch and build cannot, since
the hyphen is the field separator. Matching a bare "^${p}-" prefix would
therefore report kernel_armv8-mac-headers-6.18.33-aarch64-1 as a match for
kernel_armv8-mac. Anchoring the three trailing hyphen-separated fields
distinguishes them.

The package list mirrors the intent of the Arch and Fedora ones -- kernel,
boot, firmware, audio, graphics and the Touch Bar -- using the names under
which those components are packaged for Slackware on Apple Silicon.

asahi-diagnose is #!/bin/sh, so the helper avoids bashisms; it parses clean
under `sh -n`.

--- a/asahi-diagnose
+++ b/asahi-diagnose
@@ -144,6 +144,19 @@
 }


+# Slackware has no query command that accepts a list of package names, so read
+# the package database directly and let the caller's `$cmd $pkgs` shape stand.
+#
+# A Slackware package file is name-version-arch-build, and only the NAME may
+# contain hyphens. Anchoring the three trailing hyphen-separated fields is
+# therefore what distinguishes kernel_armv8-mac from kernel_armv8-mac-headers;
+# a bare "^${p}-" prefix match would report the headers package as the kernel.
+slackware_pkgs() {
+    for p in "$@"; do
+      ls /var/log/packages/ 2>/dev/null | grep -E "^${p}-[^-]+-[^-]+-[^-]+$"
+    done
+}
+
 package_versions() {
     echo "## Package versions"
     if [ -e /etc/arch-release ]; then
@@ -158,6 +171,13 @@
             fedora-asahi-remix-scripts tiny-dfr uboot-images-armv8 kernel-16k
             kernel-16k-modules-extra asahi-fwextract dracut-asahi update-m1n1
             asahi-audio speakersafetyd wireplumber pipewire mesa"
+    elif [ -e /etc/slackware-version ]; then
+      cmd="slackware_pkgs"
+      pkgs="kernel_armv8-mac asahi-scripts asahi-fwextract lzfse
+            alsa-ucm-conf-asahi asahi-audio speakersafetyd tiny-dfr hwm-bw-mac
+            mesa pipewire wireplumber
+            lv2 lilv serd sord sratom zix
+            bankstown triforce-lv2 lsp-plugins-lv2"
     else
       echo "Distribution not supported"
       return
